RPC signatures for Koda (`lib/ai/contracts.ts`):

```typescript
// get_studio_ai_budget_usage
// supabase.rpc('get_studio_ai_budget_usage', { p_studio_id: string, p_days?: number })
interface AiBudgetUsage {
  total_cost_cents: number;        // bigint from DB, JS number
  cap_cents: number;               // 500 × p_days
  budget_remaining_cents: number;  // GREATEST(cap - total, 0)
  days: number;
  job_count: number;
}

// record_ai_cost  (service_role / workers only — never call from app routes)
// supabase.rpc('record_ai_cost', {
//   p_studio_id: string,
//   p_job_id: string,
//   p_job_type: 'reply_draft' | 'consult_summary' | 'aftercare_gen',
//   p_model: string,
//   p_input_tokens: number,
//   p_output_tokens: number,
//   p_cost_cents: number,
// })
// Returns: void
// Side effects: inserts ai_costs row + updates ai_jobs (status='done', completed_at, token counts)
```

One schema note: `ai_voice_profiles` uses `UNIQUE NULLS NOT DISTINCT (studio_id, artist_id)` — this is Postgres 15+ syntax. Supabase cloud runs PG15 so it's fine. Semantics: one studio-level profile (artist_id IS NULL) plus one per studio+artist combo, all enforced by the unique index.
